# Vendored engine sources - the pin record.
#
# Format: <name> <upstream-commit-or-tag> <license-id> <upstream-url>
#
# One uncommented line per vendor/<name>/ tree. The four fields are machine-read
# by generate_release_sbom.rb (`parse_vendor_pins`) and ai_package_gate.rb, and
# `<name>` must equal the directory name. Everything else on this page is a
# comment, including the per-pin detail blocks - a commented line is NOT a pin,
# deliberately, so an intended-but-not-yet-imported pin cannot be mistaken for
# shipped bytes.
#
# Three rules this file exists to enforce:
#
#   1. ONE SHARED ggml. llama.cpp and whisper.cpp each bundle their own copy
#      upstream; vendoring both as-is means duplicate symbols and doubled binary
#      size. Both are built against the single ggml pinned here.
#   2. PERMISSIVE ONLY. Every pin is MIT, BSD or Apache-2.0. A copyleft
#      dependency can never enter this package - ai_package_gate.rb checks the
#      licence id against the schema's copyleft dimension, which exists because
#      espeak-ng (GPL-3.0) sits one transitive hop from a TTS build graph.
#   3. PINNED, NEVER FLOATING. Unpinned is chaos and frozen is rot, so the pins
#      move through a bump PR that runs the full gate set.
#
# The trees are COMMITTED, not fetched at sync. SPM builds these as SOURCE
# targets, and a source target has to exist in the mirror repository at the tag
# a consumer resolves - there is no fetch step in `swift package resolve` that
# could pull them in. The cost is a few megabytes in the repo; the alternative
# is a package that cannot be installed. Import procedure, prune lists and the
# two vendor patches: docs/vendoring.md.
#
# ── ggml ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The single shared tensor library. Copied from llama.cpp's `ggml/` subtree at
# the llama pin below, which upstream had synced from ggml-org/ggml at exactly
# this commit; whisper.cpp's bundled copy was synced from the SAME commit, so
# the de-duplication needed no version reconciliation at all. The kept files are
# byte-identical between the two upstreams except one CPU op that llama's copy
# additionally supports (GGML_OP_CONV_2D), i.e. llama's copy is a superset.
#   commit date: 2026-07-30 - "ggml : bump version to 0.18.0" (ggml 0.18.0)
#   pruned: everything except CMakeLists.txt, cmake/, include/, and the core
#           sources plus the three backends this package ships - ggml-cpu,
#           ggml-metal (Apple GPU), ggml-blas (Accelerate on Apple). Removed:
#           ggml-cuda, ggml-hip, ggml-musa, ggml-sycl, ggml-vulkan, ggml-opencl,
#           ggml-cann, ggml-rpc, ggml-webgpu, ggml-zdnn, ggml-zendnn, ggml-et,
#           ggml-hexagon, ggml-openvino, ggml-virtgpu. Inside ggml-cpu: the
#           kleidiai backend (its CMake DOWNLOADS a tarball from the network at
#           configure time, which a vendored offline build cannot have), the
#           spacemit RISC-V vendor kernels, and arch/{loongarch,powerpc,riscv,
#           s390,wasm} - no Despia target platform is any of those.
#   patched: CMakeLists.txt - the git-derived build stamp now yields to a value
#           the embedder passes in. Vendored, `git rev-parse HEAD` here reports
#           the EMBEDDING repo's commit, so the library was self-reporting a
#           version string unrelated to its own code (and flipping to "-dirty"
#           on unrelated edits). The top-level CMakeLists feeds it this pin.
ggml         06ca97616793248fadb410ea8d69c7511b2005e4  MIT  https://github.com/ggml-org/ggml
